sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Signed-in user
    participant CK as Cookie authentication
    participant AP as AuthCookiePrincipal.RevalidateAsync
    participant US as IUserAccountStore
    participant DB as MarsvinDb
    participant AZ as Authorization
    participant PG as The requested page

    Note over U,PG: Runs on EVERY request that carries the login cookie, before any page code.<br/>The cookie is only a snapshot from sign-in - this is what keeps it true.

    U->>CK: any request + auth cookie
    CK->>CK: decrypt and check the signature
    alt cookie missing, tampered with, or idle for more than 30 minutes
        CK-->>U: treated as not signed in
    else cookie valid
        CK->>AP: OnValidatePrincipal(principal)
        AP->>US: FindById(userId from the cookie)
        US->>DB: SELECT ... FROM Users WHERE UserId = @UserId
        DB-->>US: account, or nothing
        US-->>AP: ApplicationUser or null

        alt account deleted, or IsActive = false
            AP-->>CK: RejectPrincipal + SignOut
            Note over AP: An admin deactivating an account<br/>takes effect on its very next click.
        else the cookie's stamp differs from Users.SecurityStamp
            AP-->>CK: RejectPrincipal + SignOut
            Note over AP: The stamp is replaced when the password is changed<br/>or reset, and by "log out everywhere".<br/>Every older cookie - a stolen one included - dies here.
        else signed in more than 8 hours ago
            AP-->>CK: RejectPrincipal + SignOut
            Note over AP: The 30 minutes are sliding, so on their own a session<br/>in constant use would never end. This is the hard limit.
        else role, name or email changed since sign-in
            AP->>AP: Build(user, original sign-in time)
            AP-->>CK: ReplacePrincipal, renew the cookie
            Note over AP: A demoted Admin loses /Admin on this request.<br/>The sign-in time is kept - a change never buys more time.
        else nothing changed
            AP-->>CK: keep the principal<br/>(cookie renewed, so the 30 minutes count from this request)
        end

        opt session kept, and the marsvin-lang cookie (da / en) differs from Users.PrefersEnglish
            AP->>US: SetPrefersEnglish(userId, english)
            Note over AP,US: So emails this user does not trigger themselves<br/>are in the language they read the site in.<br/>Any other cookie value is ignored.
        end

        CK->>AZ: principal, or anonymous
        alt page is on the public list
            AZ->>PG: run the handler
        else not signed in
            AZ-->>U: Redirect to /Account/Login
        else signed in, role not allowed on this page
            AZ-->>U: Redirect to /Account/AccessDenied
        else allowed
            AZ->>PG: run the handler
            PG-->>U: page, sent with Cache-Control: no-store
            Note over PG,U: So the Back button cannot bring a profile<br/>or an order back after logging out.
        end
    end

    Note over U,PG: Deny by default: a page is public only if Program.cs lists it.<br/>A new page that forgets its [Authorize] ends up behind the login.
